ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: recall.seq.feedback
display_id: SEQ-RECALL-FEEDBACK
module: recall
title: Record recall feedback and use
summary: Updates a memory's helped and hurt counts and its last use from agent feedback, deliberate use,
  or sleep's verdicts on recalled memories.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: The agent reports on or uses a memory, or a sleep run reports verdicts
operation: recall.op.feedback
participants:
- id: caller
  is:
  - actor.agent
  - consolidation.seq.sleep
  label: Agent or sleep run
- sys.daemon
- id: db
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Stack database
items:
- msg:
    from: caller
    to: sys.daemon
    text: Report on a memory
    call: Kernle.feedback(memory_id, verdict, note)
    inputs:
    - name: memory_id
      source: The caller
      source_kind: parameter
    - name: verdict
      source: 'The caller: helped, wrong, outdated; from sleep also hurt or irrelevant; or a deliberate
        use'
      source_kind: parameter
    invokes:
    - stacks.seq.resolve
- msg:
    from: sys.daemon
    to: db
    text: Find the memory in the caller's stack
    ops:
    - op: read
      entity: memory.data.memory
      by:
      - id
- alt:
    branches:
    - when: the memory is not in the stack
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: caller
          text: Not found
          reply: true
          results:
          - code: not_found
    - when: the verdict is helped
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Count the help and the use
          ops:
          - op: upsert
            entity: recall.data.usage
            by:
            - memory_id
            set:
            - helped_count + 1
            - last_feedback_at now
          - op: update
            entity: memory.data.memory
            by:
            - id
            set:
            - last_used_at now
            - times_accessed + 1
    - when: the verdict is wrong, outdated or hurt
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Count the harm; the memory itself is unchanged
          ops:
          - op: upsert
            entity: recall.data.usage
            by:
            - memory_id
            set:
            - hurt_count + 1
            - last_feedback_at now
    - when: the call is a deliberate use
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: db
          text: Count the use
          call: Kernle.record_access(memory_type, memory_id)
          ops:
          - op: update
            entity: memory.data.memory
            by:
            - id
            set:
            - last_used_at now
            - times_accessed + 1
    - when: the verdict is irrelevant
      items:
      - note:
          over:
          - sys.daemon
          text: No count changes
- msg:
    from: sys.daemon
    to: db
    text: Record the outcome
    ops:
    - op: insert
      entity: recall.data.recall-log
      set:
      - tier = feedback
      - memory_id
      - outcome
      - session_id
      - created_at now
      - expires_at
- msg:
    from: sys.daemon
    to: caller
    text: Recorded
    reply: true
rationale: Helpfulness, not exposure, keeps a memory alive and ranks it higher. Wrong or outdated feedback
  never edits or deletes the memory, because the feedback may itself come from a manipulated agent; it
  only lowers ranking, and deletion stays with retention and the owner. A wrong verdict also becomes evidence
  for the next sleep, which can revise the memory through its own policy.
